  "description": "Depot's rules every client answers alike (ADR 0155 decision 7.3, § Depot's move): `view` — what an opened file is (the core's FileView.decide as the web reads it: the web draws an SVG, so its `svg` is on), `folderPlan` — a picked directory's plan (FolderUpload: each name safe, told apart by slug per directory, the top numbered among the level's siblings; `tokens` are the folding's answers the plan may ask, [kind, name, token], and a client fails a case where it asks one not listed), `raster` — an SVG's canvas within the caps (SvgView.plan; a null ratio is NaN), `zoom` — the zoom steps. Inputs are kept; every `expected` and a plan's `tokens` are written by the core's DepotVectorsTest (VEYQ_WRITE_VECTORS=1 ./gradlew :apps:depot:jvmTest --tests '*DepotVectorsTest*'). Read through @veyq/core-js/depot by the package's depot.test.ts and through the web's glue by features/depot/vectors.test.ts.",
